what is up ladies and gentlemen boys and  girls of all ages it is Jerry and it's  time once again for some first  impression um I just got out of  transcendence which is the new film  directed by longtime cinematographer  Wally Pfister you probably know a lot of  his work from most of Christopher  Nolan's films and the ton of other stuff  he's done but this is his debut as a  director and um it's a pretty  interesting movie this i'm going to  start someplace different just because i  feel the need to this movie kind of  illustrates again what I don't like  about aggregate rating systems like  rotten tomatoes because while this movie  is not perfect I really think nineteen  percent is a pretty poor indicator for  the quality level of this movie but  anyhow on to the film itself  transcendence is definitely an ambitious  movie you get the sense that Wally  Pfister wants to make a you know a big  splash with his directorial debut and I  do gotta give the film credit for that  because it's mixed and and and in some  cases like really negative as some of  the reviews have been here I do always  prefer a movie that has too many  ambitions to a film that's you know just  lazy and this film isn't lazy by any  stretch i don't i don't think this is a  sort of ethically concerned science  fiction movie it has a lot of questions  about you know human consciousness  versus artificial intelligence and you  know when is too much technology and too  much blurring of the line between  consciousness and technology a bad thing  or a good thing or any of that first of  all you know the cast in this movie for  the most part is really spot-on rebecca  hall is fantastic paul bettany is  fantastic it's nice to see johnny depp  acting again in a role that isn't Jack  Sparrow or a similar kind of thing I  like Jack Sparrow and and I even like  The Lone Ranger but it seems like those  characters are really easy for him to do  and really fun for him to do but I've  been wanting him to go back to a little  bit more  of a serious role for a while and at  least as I'm feeling right now he does  come across as kinda rusty in this movie  which is a bummer but he's not bad I  don't think it bad but I certainly hope  he does more of these sorts of films  shake that rust off and the rest the  cast is good you know Morgan Freeman's  in here Killian Murphy's in here except  a collins jr. pops up Josh Stewart pops  up who I love I hope he continues to get  work a lot of people you know are on  loan from the Christopher Nolan  wheelhouse and um the film itself is  alright I like it there's definitely  stuff to be admired here there's a lot  of gorgeous cinematography there was  some really cool effects but beyond that  I mean there are some really great  scenes there are some really great  performances there are some beautiful  and interesting ideas and there are some  palpably scary and unsettling ideas and  it doesn't feel totally like your  stereotypical oh there is some really  wonderful human stuff in here and that's  definitely to be appreciated it's not  you know your big loud you know like a  sci-fi movie you know there's a bit of  action here and there but it's certainly  not a blow on me by any strategy does it  always work no partly because there are  times when at least I got pulled out  kind of thinking we'll wait a minute I  get that you're sort of set in a version  of the world where these things are  possible but you kind of gotta at least  fill in some of the gaps to me the stuff  that kind of hampers this movie from  time to time is basically the sense that  the ideas it wants to explore our  perhaps bigger than the intelligence of  the script itself there are certain  times where I found myself getting  caught up on like wait a minute why  didn't somebody catch this or how did  this become possible now there are times  when it seems like it's sort of counting  on you just to fill in the gaps and  sometimes that the pacing is a little  uneven but I definitely like it more  than I don't and there are a lot of  things to appreciate about it it's  definitely worth checking out I'm  interested to see how I'm going to feel  tomorrow when we sit down and do the  actual review and I'm interested to see  how I'm gonna feeling in a week or two  it's certainly worth checking out it  brings up some interesting ideas and it  does have an elegant touch with at least  some of them it does succeed on  some levels if it doesn't succeed on all  of them so I think it does certainly  deserve some credit it's not like a you  know [ __ ] waste of time by any  stretch of the imagination there is a  lot of care and effort in here it  doesn't always come across as capable of  selling and really coming to conclusions  on the idea as it puts out there all the  time and that's an element that sort of  always seems a bit problematic with  movies like these we've created a  computer with an artificial  intelligences doing things that we would  never have been capable of and it's  omnipresent and it's everywhere and it's  creating new technology and I feel like  that can sort of back a filmmaker into a  corner in terms of how can we make it  plausible when anyone takes a stand  against this thing so these movies have  a tendency to kind of pile stuff on and  get really really big in terms of  implications and things that start  happening and that chain reaction isn't  bad and there is some really cool stuff  that comes out of it but especially  toward the end there a couple of moments  where you're like whoa wait hold on a  second what you know but um there's  certainly some stuff that's worth  checking out here everyone involved  seems really committed and really into  it there's a lot of tender loving care  that went into this movie it seems like  it's not entirely successful but it's  worth checking out it does give you  something to think about and some stuff  to talk about and for someone who's a  first-time director with a film of t